हर हुनर की पहचान, हर मेहनत का सम्मान।

1. Problem Statement
Twenty Years of Skill, No Way to Prove It
A painter, carpenter, tailor, or electrician may have decades of practical experience but no reliable digital record to prove it. Many workers depend on word-of-mouth recommendations to find jobs. When they move to a new city, they may have to rebuild their reputation from scratch.

Customers face a similar problem: they often have no easy way to judge a worker's experience, reliability, or previous work.

2. What Did We Build?
We developed Shramik, a digital platform concept that helps skilled workers create a professional identity and maintain a record of their skills and completed jobs.

Workers can showcase their experience through shareable profiles and QR codes. Customer-confirmed jobs can provide additional evidence of completed work, helping workers build credibility and giving potential customers more confidence.

3. Why Did We Build It?
We believe that practical skills deserve recognition, regardless of educational background or access to technology.

Shramik aims to solve the problem of undocumented work experience by making professional records easier to create, maintain, and share.

4. Key Features
👷 Digital Worker Profiles: Showcase skills and experience.
🛠️ Skills Record: Display professional trades and abilities.
📋 Work History: Maintain records of completed jobs.
✅ Customer Confirmation: Support credibility through confirmed work.
🔗 Shareable Profiles: Share professional information through a link.
📱 QR Codes: Make profiles easier to access and share.
🔒 Privacy-Focused Design: Help workers control the information they share.
5. How Does Shramik Work?
A worker creates a digital profile.
The worker adds skills and relevant experience.
Completed jobs are recorded on the profile.
Customers confirm jobs through the supported confirmation process.
The worker shares their profile or QR code with potential customers.
Customers can review the available information before deciding whom to hire.
6. Our Mission
To help skilled workers prove their experience, build trust, and access better opportunities through a simple and accessible digital identity.

7. Our Vision
A future where every skilled worker has a way to showcase their abilities and receive recognition for their hard work.

Shramik — Every skill deserves recognition. 🧡

APP ARCHITECTURE

mermaid-diagram (3) FLOW CHART ### `01` Entry Point
index.ts initializes the Express backend, configures middleware and CORS, and registers API route handlers.

The frontend uses main.tsx and App.tsx to initialize and render the React application.

02 Authentication Flow
Routes: auth.ts handles registration and login endpoints (when implemented).
Services: authService.ts manages authentication-related business logic.
Helpers: Password hashing and token management can be added to secure user accounts.
User Roles: Shramik supports separate experiences for workers and customers.
Database: User and authentication data can be stored persistently once a database is integrated.
03 Protected Routes
Protected routes can restrict access to authenticated users based on their roles.

Worker routes: Worker profiles, availability, jobs, and bookings.
Customer routes: Worker discovery, service bookings, and booking history.
Authentication middleware: Validates user sessions or JWTs when authentication is implemented.
04 Worker & Customer Management
Worker profiles: Store trade, skills, experience, and service information.
Customer management: Support customer profiles and service requests.
Worker discovery: Help customers find professionals by service category and location.
Availability: Allow workers to manage available booking slots.
Bookings: Support booking creation, confirmation, and status management.
Database persistence and API integration are required for these features to work reliably across sessions.

05 Booking & Location Integration
Routes: Worker, job, booking, and location endpoints can be organized under the backend routes directory.
Services: Dedicated services handle worker discovery, booking logic, and location-related operations.
Location selection: Users can choose an area or provide location details.
Distance filtering: Accurate nearby-worker search requires real coordinates and distance calculations.
Booking flow: Customers select a worker, date, and available time slot.
06 AI Assistant
Shramik Sahayak uses the Gemini API integration to provide AI-powered assistance when configured.

Chat API: Receives user messages through the backend.
Gemini integration: Generates responses using the configured API key.
User guidance: Helps users navigate the platform and understand available features.
API keys should remain on the server and must never be committed to GitHub.

07 Background Jobs & Notifications
Background processing can be introduced to support:

Booking reminders and status notifications.
Availability updates.
Scheduled cleanup tasks.
Other asynchronous operations as the platform grows.
A queue system such as BullMQ with Redis is an optional future enhancement, not a required part of the initial prototype.

08 Deployment & Automation
GitHub Actions can automate build checks, testing, and deployment workflows.

Continuous integration: Run linting and build checks when code changes.
Deployment: Publish the frontend and backend to configured hosting services.
Environment configuration: Store API keys and other secrets securely in deployment settings.
Scheduled workflows: Add cron-based tasks only when the application requires them.
The exact workflow depends on the hosting setup and the services implemented in the project.

08 Data Layer
Data Management & Persistence — Shramik uses a structured data layer to manage worker profiles, customer information, skills, job listings, and bookings. A database and ORM can be integrated to support reliable data storage and type-safe database operations.

