## API Reference
API endpoints for connecting workers, customers, bookings, and AI assistance

Note: These endpoints are a proposed API structure for Shramik. Update the table to match the routes actually implemented in your backend.

GET Endpoints
Endpoint	Description
/api/workers	Retrieve the list of available workers
/api/workers/:id	Get details of a specific worker
/api/workers/:id/availability	View a worker's available time slots
/api/bookings	Retrieve bookings for the authenticated user
/api/bookings/:id	Get details of a specific booking
/api/jobs	Retrieve available job opportunities for workers
/api/locations	Retrieve supported service locations
/api/health	Check backend service health
POST Endpoints
Endpoint	Description
/api/auth/register	Register a new customer or worker
/api/auth/login	Authenticate a registered user
/api/workers	Create a worker profile
/api/bookings	Create a service booking
/api/jobs	Post a job opportunity
/api/reviews	Submit a review for a completed service
/api/chat	Send a message to Shramik Sahayak AI
PATCH Endpoints
Endpoint	Description
/api/workers/:id	Update worker profile details
/api/workers/:id/availability	Update worker availability
/api/bookings/:id/status	Update booking status
/api/jobs/:id/status	Update job status
DELETE Endpoints
Endpoint	Description
/api/bookings/:id	Cancel a booking, subject to authorization rules
/api/jobs/:id	Remove a job posting, subject to authorization rules
Authentication and authorization: Protected endpoints should require an authenticated session or a valid token, such as Authorization: Bearer <token>, if JWT authentication is implemented. Users should only be able to access or modify records they are authorized to manage.

Database Schema
Suggested data model for connecting customers and skilled workers

Table	Purpose
users	Store account details and user roles
worker_profiles	Store skills, experience, service areas, and profile information
services	Maintain categories such as plumbing, painting, carpentry, and electrical work
availability_slots	Store worker availability
bookings	Track service requests, schedules, and booking statuses
jobs	Store job opportunities posted by customers
reviews	Store customer feedback and ratings
locations	Store supported service areas
chat_sessions	Store AI conversation metadata, if persistence is implemented
Data integrity: Use unique identifiers, timestamps, appropriate relationships, and authorization checks. Personal information should be collected only when necessary and protected from unauthorized access.

The tables above describe a proposed schema. They should not be presented as existing database tables until the database and migrations have been implemented.

Deployment
Suggested deployment architecture for Shramik

Component	Possible Platform
Frontend	Vercel or Netlify
Backend API	Render or Railway
Database	PostgreSQL on a managed database service, if configured
AI Assistance	Google Gemini API
File Storage	Cloudinary or another storage service, if profile uploads are supported
Background Jobs	Redis-backed queue, if asynchronous jobs are implemented
Monitoring	Hosting-provider logs and an error-monitoring service
Frontend and backend deployments should be configured with the correct API URL, environment variables, CORS rules, and production build settings. Never expose secret API keys in frontend code.

Project Limitations & Assumptions
Shramik focuses on connecting customers with informal skilled workers in service categories such as plumbing, electrical work, painting, carpentry, tailoring, and masonry.
The interface is designed to support Hindi and English.
Worker availability and booking features depend on the backend and data persistence being configured correctly.
Location-based search depends on the accuracy of the location data and the implementation of distance calculations.
Worker identity verification should not be described as active unless a verification process has been implemented and tested.
Ratings and reviews should represent genuine customer feedback, not sample or placeholder data.
AI assistance depends on a valid Gemini API key, network access, API availability, and appropriate error handling.
Database persistence, authentication, notifications, background jobs, and deployment integrations depend on the services actually configured.
Shramik is an independent platform concept and should not be represented as affiliated with a government agency unless an official partnership exists.
Users should be informed how their contact details, location, and booking information are used and protected.
Future Improvements
Implement secure registration, login, and role-based authorization.
Add persistent storage for users, worker profiles, bookings, and reviews.
Introduce a transparent worker verification process.
Improve location-based worker discovery and service-area filtering.
Add booking notifications and booking-status updates.
Expand Shramik Sahayak with multilingual assistance and helpful service guidance.
Add accessibility improvements for users with limited digital literacy.
Introduce reporting and moderation tools to help address fraudulent profiles and inappropriate behavior.
About
Shramik (श्रमिक) is a skill-and-service platform concept designed to help customers discover local skilled workers and help workers find service opportunities.

Tagline: Skill · Work · Trust

Hindi motto: हर हुनर की पहचान, हर मेहनत का सम्मान।

The goal is to make finding work and hiring skilled workers simpler, more accessible, and more transparent.

Acknowledgements
Built with the aim of making local work opportunities easier to discover and helping every skill receive the recognition it deserves.
